  <Patch Id="NCdbcDGRIQBtzDa8Qsjck9">
    <Canvas Id="x446rPzz3AoiThXTUwistN" DefaultCategory="Main" BordersChecked="false" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,180" Id="rm9eKIEmpaF75V7Im2Uaem">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <CategoryReference Kind="Category" Name="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="1FhshkNfPiVAOgARb5Xv4o">
        <Canvas Id="VakVFEiIWqygU31A4k81W4" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="87lNBG4e1T4NB97adIxa8G" Bounds="85,16,420,52" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="How To Chain Effects">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">25</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="7FWqnojcfaXzr3VWh4Tmpi" Bounds="85,85,523,124" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Effect nodes (Qt.Effects) on the Effect pin&#xD;&#xA;- Chain them: Output to Input, the last one to the Effect pin&#xD;&#xA;- One chain can feed several elements&#xD;&#xA;- Blur, DropShadow, ColorAdjust, Colorize, Mask share one layer&#xD;&#xA;- A shader node (RGBSplit) gets a layer of its own&#xD;&#xA;- Order across a shader changes the picture">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="6Rha6yqGSHebm8tcNGbspp" Bounds="85,955,830,286" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Neighbouring MultiEffect nodes (Blur, DropShadow, ColorAdjust, Colorize, Mask; category Qt.Effects.MultiEffect) are folded into ONE Qt MultiEffect: one layer, one shader. Inside such a run Qt's fixed order applies, the order of the nodes does not matter.&#xD;&#xA;- A shader node (category Qt.Effects, e.g. RGBSplit or Glow) never shares a layer: it ends the run and costs at least one offscreen layer of its own. A shader between Blur and DropShadow costs three layers (example 1), Blur and DropShadow on one side of it would share one (example 3). Between the runs the data flow order applies, like Stride TextureFX: the first node of the chain works first, the node at the Effect pin works last. Examples 1 and 2 use the same three nodes in opposite order.&#xD;&#xA;- The cost is the number of layers (an offscreen texture plus a render pass): keep MultiEffect nodes together and, where the look allows it, put shader nodes at the start or the end of a chain.&#xD;&#xA;- Size, Transform and Interaction stay on the element, not on the effects. The same chain can feed several elements: in example 3 the Rectangle takes the Blur output, the Text the DropShadow output.&#xD;&#xA;- Padding: with Auto Padding on (default) the layer grows automatically. Optional pins: Blur Max and Multiplier, DropShadow Scale, Auto Padding and Padding on Blur and DropShadow. If Auto Padding is off on any Blur or DropShadow, the whole layer uses the largest Padding per side of all of them.&#xD;&#xA;- A shader that draws beyond the element (RGBSplit shifts the colors outwards) sets @padding in the head of the .frag, in DIP: one number or left, top, right, bottom; otherwise the effect may be clipped at the element bounds. A shader node shows compile errors with line numbers at its Error output.&#xD;&#xA;- How filter shader files become nodes: see HowTo Create Shader Nodes from Files.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="bn3X8N66xNNaKlyWGxHsrc" Bounds="100,235,450,46" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="1  Blur -&gt; RGBSplit -&gt; DropShadow: the blurred text is split into its color channels, the shadow follows the result.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
